{"v":15,"id":"e14","kid":"emma","title":"My First Week at a Canadian Middle School","zh":"我在加拿大中学的第一周","level":"A2+","genre":"留学生活","src":"original","sum":"李娜在卡尔加里上中学的第一周博客：走班上课常迷路、课堂上大家爱提问讨论、午饭时间短、参加了羽毛球队。虽有困难，她学着对自己耐心一点。","words":303,"paras":[{"t":"Hi everyone! It's me, Li Na. I promised to write about my first week at Maple Grove Middle School in Calgary, so here it is.","w":[[0,2,"hi",-1],[3,11,"everyone",-1],[13,17,"it's",-1],[18,20,"me",-1],[22,24,"Li",0],[25,27,"Na",0],[29,30,"i",-1],[31,39,"promised",-1],[40,42,"to",-1],[43,48,"write",-1],[49,54,"about",-1],[55,57,"my",-1],[58,63,"first",-1],[64,68,"week",-1],[69,71,"at",-1],[72,77,"Maple",1],[78,83,"Grove",1],[84,90,"middle",1],[91,97,"school",1],[98,100,"in",-1],[101,108,"Calgary",-1],[110,112,"so",-1],[113,117,"here",2],[118,120,"it",2],[121,123,"is",2]]},{"t":"The first surprise was the schedule. In China, we stayed in the same classroom and the teachers came to us. Here, every student has a locker, and we move to a different room for each subject. The hallways are crazy between classes! On my first day, I got lost twice and arrived late for math. Luckily, the teacher, Mr. Thompson, just smiled and said, \"Welcome! Take a seat anywhere.\"","w":[[0,3,"the",-1],[4,9,"first",-1],[10,18,"surprise",-1],[19,22,"was",-1],[23,26,"the",-1],[27,35,"schedule",-1],[37,39,"in",-1],[40,45,"china",-1],[47,49,"we",-1],[50,56,"stayed",-1],[57,59,"in",-1],[60,63,"the",-1],[64,68,"same",-1],[69,78,"classroom",-1],[79,82,"and",-1],[83,86,"the",-1],[87,95,"teachers",-1],[96,100,"came",-1],[101,103,"to",-1],[104,106,"us",-1],[108,112,"here",-1],[114,119,"every",-1],[120,127,"student",-1],[128,131,"has",-1],[132,133,"a",-1],[134,140,"locker",-1],[142,145,"and",-1],[146,148,"we",-1],[149,153,"move",-1],[154,156,"to",-1],[157,158,"a",-1],[159,168,"different",-1],[169,173,"room",-1],[174,177,"for",-1],[178,182,"each",-1],[183,190,"subject",-1],[192,195,"the",-1],[196,204,"hallways",-1],[205,208,"are",-1],[209,214,"crazy",-1],[215,222,"between",-1],[223,230,"classes",-1],[232,234,"on",-1],[235,237,"my",-1],[238,243,"first",-1],[244,247,"day",-1],[249,250,"i",-1],[251,254,"got",3],[255,259,"lost",3],[260,265,"twice",-1],[266,269,"and",-1],[270,277,"arrived",-1],[278,282,"late",-1],[283,286,"for",-1],[287,291,"math",-1],[293,300,"luckily",-1],[302,305,"the",-1],[306,313,"teacher",-1],[315,318,"Mr",18],[319,327,"Thompson",18],[329,333,"just",-1],[334,340,"smiled",-1],[341,344,"and",-1],[345,349,"said",-1],[352,359,"welcome",-1],[361,365,"take",4],[366,367,"a",4],[368,372,"seat",4],[373,381,"anywhere",-1]]},{"t":"The second surprise was the way classes work. Students ask lots of questions and sometimes even disagree with the teacher. In social studies, we sat in groups and discussed whether our city should build more bike lanes. I was too nervous to talk at first, but my group was patient. When I finally shared my idea, a boy named Owen said, \"That's a really good point.\" I felt great.","w":[[0,3,"the",-1],[4,10,"second",-1],[11,19,"surprise",-1],[20,23,"was",-1],[24,27,"the",-1],[28,31,"way",-1],[32,39,"classes",-1],[40,44,"work",-1],[46,54,"students",-1],[55,58,"ask",-1],[59,63,"lots",17],[64,66,"of",17],[67,76,"questions",-1],[77,80,"and",-1],[81,90,"sometimes",-1],[91,95,"even",-1],[96,104,"disagree",-1],[105,109,"with",-1],[110,113,"the",-1],[114,121,"teacher",-1],[123,125,"in",-1],[126,132,"social",5],[133,140,"studies",5],[142,144,"we",-1],[145,148,"sat",-1],[149,151,"in",-1],[152,158,"groups",-1],[159,162,"and",-1],[163,172,"discussed",-1],[173,180,"whether",-1],[181,184,"our",-1],[185,189,"city",-1],[190,196,"should",-1],[197,202,"build",-1],[203,207,"more",-1],[208,212,"bike",6],[213,218,"lanes",6],[220,221,"i",-1],[222,225,"was",-1],[226,229,"too",-1],[230,237,"nervous",-1],[238,240,"to",-1],[241,245,"talk",-1],[246,248,"at",7],[249,254,"first",7],[256,259,"but",-1],[260,262,"my",-1],[263,268,"group",-1],[269,272,"was",-1],[273,280,"patient",-1],[282,286,"when",-1],[287,288,"i",-1],[289,296,"finally",-1],[297,303,"shared",-1],[304,306,"my",-1],[307,311,"idea",-1],[313,314,"a",-1],[315,318,"boy",-1],[319,324,"named",-1],[325,329,"Owen",-1],[330,334,"said",-1],[337,343,"that's",-1],[344,345,"a",-1],[346,352,"really",-1],[353,357,"good",8],[358,363,"point",8],[366,367,"i",-1],[368,372,"felt",-1],[373,378,"great",-1]]},{"t":"Lunch is short, only thirty minutes, and most students bring their own lunch from home. On Tuesday I brought fried rice in a food jar, and two girls asked to try it. Now they want me to teach them how to use chopsticks!","w":[[0,5,"lunch",-1],[6,8,"is",-1],[9,14,"short",-1],[16,20,"only",-1],[21,27,"thirty",-1],[28,35,"minutes",-1],[37,40,"and",-1],[41,45,"most",-1],[46,54,"students",-1],[55,60,"bring",-1],[61,66,"their",-1],[67,70,"own",-1],[71,76,"lunch",-1],[77,81,"from",-1],[82,86,"home",-1],[88,90,"on",-1],[91,98,"tuesday",-1],[99,100,"i",-1],[101,108,"brought",-1],[109,114,"fried",9],[115,119,"rice",9],[120,122,"in",-1],[123,124,"a",-1],[125,129,"food",10],[130,133,"jar",10],[135,138,"and",-1],[139,142,"two",-1],[143,148,"girls",-1],[149,154,"asked",-1],[155,157,"to",-1],[158,161,"try",-1],[162,164,"it",-1],[166,169,"now",-1],[170,174,"they",-1],[175,179,"want",-1],[180,182,"me",-1],[183,185,"to",-1],[186,191,"teach",-1],[192,196,"them",-1],[197,200,"how",-1],[201,203,"to",-1],[204,207,"use",-1],[208,218,"chopsticks",-1]]},{"t":"After school, there are lots of clubs and teams. I joined the badminton team and the art club. Badminton practice is on Mondays and Wednesdays, and I think I'm one of the better players. (Thank you, Dad, for all those weekends in the park!)","w":[[0,5,"after",-1],[6,12,"school",-1],[14,19,"there",-1],[20,23,"are",-1],[24,28,"lots",17],[29,31,"of",17],[32,37,"clubs",-1],[38,41,"and",-1],[42,47,"teams",-1],[49,50,"i",-1],[51,57,"joined",-1],[58,61,"the",-1],[62,71,"badminton",11],[72,76,"team",11],[77,80,"and",-1],[81,84,"the",-1],[85,88,"art",12],[89,93,"club",12],[95,104,"badminton",-1],[105,113,